text.paragraph:
Cephalexin is active against most isolates of the following bacteria both in vitro and in clinical infections (see 
                        INDICATIONS AND USAGE
                     ):

The safety and effectiveness of cephalexin tablets in pediatric patients was established in clinical trials for the dosages described in the dosage and administration section (see 
                              DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION
                           ).

Cephalexin tablets should be administered with caution in the presence of impaired renal function (creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min, with or without dialysis). Under such conditions, careful clinical observation and laboratory studies should be made because safe dosage may be lower than that usually recommended (see 
                              DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION
                           ).

Administer the following dosing regimens for cephalexin tablets to patients with renal impairment (see 
                        PRECAUTIONS
                     ).
